    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Since state can be utilized as a merging key without being set as the index, we decided not to re-index the cost_living dataset. The flexibility for grouping, filtering, and reshaping operations is maintained without additional structural complexity by maintaining state as a standard column. A RangeIndex is adequate for the analysis because the dataset does not use hierarchical indexing or time-series slicing."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "C9R-1b61jtiV"
      },
      "id": "C9R-1b61jtiV"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Handling Missing Values\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DWi5dlkbNWTC"
      },
      "id": "DWi5dlkbNWTC"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data_jobs.info()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BhFgGdeQNkVR",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "be8d0159-174a-4f11-c6a9-df8f5f79b888"
      },
      "id": "BhFgGdeQNkVR",
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "<class 'pandas.core.frame.DataFrame'>\n",
            "DatetimeIndex: 61953 entries, 2023-08-04 03:00:13.797776 to 2023-01-25 04:00:26.521124\n",
            "Data columns (total 9 columns):\n",
            " #   Column          Non-Null Count  Dtype  \n",
            "---  ------          --------------  -----  \n",
            " 0   title           61953 non-null  object \n",
            " 1   company_name    61953 non-null  object \n",
            " 2   location        61916 non-null  object \n",
            " 3   salary_hourly   5900 non-null   float64\n",
            " 4   salary_yearly   4069 non-null   float64\n",
            " 5   schedule_type   61707 non-null  object \n",
            " 6   work_from_home  27980 non-null  object \n",
            " 7   skillset        61953 non-null  object \n",
            " 8   state           17943 non-null  object \n",
            "dtypes: float64(2), object(7)\n",
            "memory usage: 4.7+ MB\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "There are NA values in the follow columns: location, salary_hourly, salary_yearly, schedule_type, work_from_home, and state."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0VyJq-GXkIBh"
      },
      "id": "0VyJq-GXkIBh"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data_jobs[\"work_from_home\"] = data_jobs[\"work_from_home\"].fillna(False)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "6DUhvoJRA3ye",
        "outputId": "f086615e-7d95-4ffe-fc71-2cb550fb5383"
      },
      "id": "6DUhvoJRA3ye",
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stderr",
          "text": [
            "/tmp/ipython-input-2306037442.py:1: FutureWarning: Downcasting object dtype arrays on .fillna, .ffill, .bfill is deprecated and will change in a future version. Call result.infer_objects(copy=False) instead. To opt-in to the future behavior, set `pd.set_option('future.no_silent_downcasting', True)`\n",
            "  data_jobs[\"work_from_home\"] = data_jobs[\"work_from_home\"].fillna(False)\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Missing work_from_home values most likely mean that the job posting did not specifically state if the position was remote. To enable consistent analysis of remote versus non-remote roles without creating ambiguity, these NaN values should be filled with False, assuming that only job ads clearly marked as remote should be handled as such."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "YJcrxTjDdp3g"
      },
      "id": "YJcrxTjDdp3g"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Replace missing schedule_type values with \"Unknown\"\n",
        "# so unreported job types are clearly labeled.\n",
        "data_jobs[\"schedule_type\"] = data_jobs[\"schedule_type\"].fillna(\"Unknown\")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pO-Woow8A_qA"
      },
      "id": "pO-Woow8A_qA",
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Replace missing state values with \"Other\"\n",
        "# to label postings without a specific state.\n",
        "data_jobs[\"state\"] = data_jobs[\"state\"].fillna(\"Other\")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "U5XND_XmxDoG"
      },
      "id": "U5XND_XmxDoG",
      "execution_count": 16,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data_jobs = data_jobs.dropna(subset=['location'])"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FLcl0GIHx85-"
      },
      "id": "FLcl0GIHx85-",
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "All remaining job posts can be assigned to a geographic category (such as state) by removing rows with missing locations. This is required for precise aggregation and merging with cost-of-living data. Because location is essential to the analysis, it is impossible to include rows without it in a meaningful way."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HVuwZlxokQA5"
      },
      "id": "HVuwZlxokQA5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# testing if filling salary NA values with 0 is appropiate\n",
        "salary_hourly_zero = data_jobs['salary_hourly'].fillna(0)\n",
        "\n",
        "zero_mean = salary_hourly_zero.mean()\n",
        "zero_median = salary_hourly_zero.median()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Mean after filling with 0:\", zero_mean)\n",
        "print(\"Median after filling with 0:\", zero_median)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10,5))\n",
        "\n",
        "sns.kdeplot(data_jobs['salary_hourly'].dropna(), label='Original (NaN ignored)')\n",
        "sns.kdeplot(salary_hourly_zero, label='NaN filled with 0')\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.title(\"Effect of Filling NaN with 0 on Salary Distribution\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 522
        },
        "id": "KlHZKFBzhAP2",
        "outputId": "ede17d6b-21f7-4e77-e335-4d4ea3e64a6b"
      },
      "id": "KlHZKFBzhAP2",
      "execution_count": 18,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Mean after filling with 0: 3.8620238710511017\n",
            "Median after filling with 0: 0.0\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Filling in missing salary numbers with 0 distorts both the mean and median, resulting in the median dropping to 0 and the mean collapsing to around 3.86. Zero is also not a legitimate wage; rather, it is missing data, as our objective is to examine real compensation trends. By adding these fictitious zeros, the salary distribution is essentially distorted, and any further study is biased."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jgaL9PH-nkVd"
      },
      "id": "jgaL9PH-nkVd"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data_jobs = data_jobs.dropna(subset=['salary_hourly', 'salary_yearly'], how='all')"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "YDqDgbWiBPRT"
      },
      "id": "YDqDgbWiBPRT",
      "execution_count": 19,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Because our analysis revolves around salary progression, it is better that rows with missing salary_hourly and salary_yearly are dropped. This preserves postings that report wage in either format while avoiding the inclusion of observations that lack useful pay data."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_-qetuwJllr4"
      },
      "id": "_-qetuwJllr4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data_jobs['salary_yearly'] = (data_jobs['salary_yearly'].fillna(data_jobs['salary_hourly'] * 2080))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mrJd4PIHvrne"
      },
      "id": "mrJd4PIHvrne",
      "execution_count": 20,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# drop salary_hourly column\n",
        "data_jobs = data_jobs.drop(columns=['salary_hourly'])"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5jp0l3D8wSVk"
      },
      "id": "5jp0l3D8wSVk",
      "execution_count": 21,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Hourly wages were converted to annual equivalents to estimate missing yearly salaries (assuming 2,080 working hours per year). This allows for uniform comparison and aggregation across job advertisements by standardizing salary into a single annual measure."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gfnuKy5imnS5"
      },
      "id": "gfnuKy5imnS5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data_jobs.head(3)"
      ],
